<article class="env-lemma" id="067Q">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/067Q">Lemma <span data-tag="067Q">31.22.7</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to Y$ and $j : Y \to X$ be immersions of schemes. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $i$ and $j$ are regular immersions, so is $j \circ i$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $i$ and $j$ are Koszul-regular immersions, so is $j \circ i$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $i$ and $j$ are $H_1$-regular immersions, so is $j \circ i$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $i$ is an $H_1$-regular immersion and $j$ is a quasi-regular immersion, then $j \circ i$ is a quasi-regular immersion. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The algebraic version of (1) is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/065K" data-tag="065K">10.68.7</a>. The algebraic version of (2) is More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0669" data-tag="0669">15.31.13</a>. The algebraic version of (3) is More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0668" data-tag="0668">15.31.11</a>. The algebraic version of (4) is More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0667" data-tag="0667">15.31.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>